; pico_ntsc — composite scanout PIO program.
;
; One state machine emits 2 bits per sample to two consecutive pins:
;   bit0 -> GPIO16 (composite SYNC, active-low: 0 = sync tip)
;   bit1 -> GPIO17 (LUMA: 1 = white, 0 = black)
; combined externally through the 560R/240R resistor DAC (PORTING.md §1.5).
;
; Autopull (threshold 32, shift right) refills the OSR, so each PIO cycle shifts
; out one 2-bit sample with no instruction overhead. At clkdiv 10 from a 126 MHz
; system clock the sample rate is 12.6 MHz.

.program ntsc

.wrap_target
    out pins, 2
.wrap
